    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0538" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2231/281a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-06">August 6, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. Stand by for detailed instructions. Proviso to concession on balsa timber
                    absolutely necessary. If agreement already signed, exchange of notes necessary.
                    If agreement not signed, proviso should be inserted in schedule II.</p>
                <p>To facilitate further instructions, telegraph that agreement has been signed if
                    that is the case.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d533-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d533-f1" n="21" xml:id="d533-f1-content">
                <p>The Minister in Ecuador in telegram No. 91, August 6, 2 p.m., stated that the
                    agreement had been signed that morning (611.2231/278).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
